sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as admin (librarian)
    participant Cat as Catalog<br/>(mfe-catalog)
    participant Hook as useAsyncAction
    participant Dash as Dashboard<br/>(mfe-admin)
    participant Api as ApiClient<br/>(shell: createApiClient)
    participant Edge as shell server<br/>(serve-frontends.mjs proxy)
    participant GW as gateway<br/>RequestIdFilter · RateLimitFilter<br/>RoutesConfig
    participant Res as CurrentMemberResolver<br/>(library-service)
    participant USC as UserServiceClient
    participant US as user-service<br/>SessionController
    participant Ctl as BookController /<br/>AdminDashboardController
    participant Svc as LibraryService
    participant Repo as InMemoryBookRepository /<br/>InMemoryAccountRepository

    Admin->>Cat: types "Dune", clicks "Add book"
    Cat->>Hook: run("add:Dune", …)
    Hook->>Api: post("/books", {title})
    Note over Api: CircuitBreaker.execute → withTimeout(8 s) → fetch<br/>(POST is never retried)
    Api->>Edge: POST /api/books (Authorization: Bearer, X-Request-Id)
    Edge->>GW: proxy(): POST /api/books + X-Forwarded-For
    Note over GW: RequestIdFilter keeps X-Request-Id<br/>RateLimitFilter → TokenBucketRateLimiter.tryConsume (429 if empty)<br/>route "library-service": StripPrefix=1, circuit breaker "libraryService"
    GW->>Res: POST /books
    Res->>USC: findByToken(token)
    USC->>US: GET /sessions/current (@Retry, @CircuitBreaker "userService")
    Note over US: SessionService.currentUser → InMemorySessionStore.resolve<br/>→ InMemoryUserRepository.findById
    US-->>USC: 200 {id:"admin", isAdmin:true}
    USC-->>Res: Member("admin", "admin", admin=true)
    Res->>Ctl: BookController.add(member, TitleRequest)
    Ctl->>Svc: addBook(member, "Dune")
    Note over Svc: actor.admin()? else ForbiddenException (403)<br/>BookTitle.of(raw) validates · takes the write lock
    Svc->>Repo: findByTitleKey("dune")
    Repo-->>Svc: empty (else BookAlreadyExistsException → 409)
    Svc->>Svc: Book.register(id, title)
    Svc->>Repo: save(book)
    Svc-->>Ctl: Book
    Ctl-->>GW: 201 AddBookResponse {message, book}
    GW-->>Edge: 201
    Edge-->>Api: 201
    Api-->>Hook: AddBookResponse
    Hook->>Hook: bus.emit("toast:show"), bus.emit("library:changed")

    par catalogue refresh
        Hook-->>Cat: library:changed
        Cat->>Api: get("/books") → … → BookController.list → LibraryService.listBooks
        Api-->>Cat: BookListResponse → re-render list
    and dashboard refresh
        Hook-->>Dash: library:changed
        Dash->>Api: get("/admin/dashboard")
        Api->>Edge: GET /api/admin/dashboard (GET: retried up to 3 times)
        Edge->>GW: proxy()
        GW->>Res: GET /admin/dashboard (same filters as above)
        Res->>USC: findByToken(token) → user-service (as steps 7–10)
        USC-->>Res: Member(admin)
        Res->>Ctl: AdminDashboardController.dashboard(member)
        Ctl->>Svc: dashboard(member)
        Note over Svc: actor.admin()? else 403 · takes the read lock
        Svc->>Repo: InMemoryBookRepository.findAll()
        Svc->>Repo: InMemoryAccountRepository.findAll()
        Note over Svc: builds AdminLoanView (ON_TIME / DUE_SOON / OVERDUE),<br/>AdminMemberView, AdminSummary → AdminDashboard
        Svc-->>Ctl: AdminDashboard
        Ctl-->>Api: 200 AdminDashboardResponse (via gateway and shell server)
        Api-->>Dash: summary, members, loans
        Dash-->>Admin: tiles + Books out / Members tables re-render
    end
